course: dictionary
lesson: 6511
title: Negotiate: talking to reach an agreement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To negotiate means to talk with someone until you both agree on something. Often each side gives a little, so both get part of what they want. «To negotiate is to talk until both people agree a deal, such as a price for a job.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «They negotiated a later bedtime», a child and a parent are talking, and the result is a new agreement. Ask what would fit: "talked and agreed" makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: Negotiate can also mean to get safely past something difficult. «The skier had to negotiate a steep, icy slope.» Nobody is making a deal here. The clues are steep and icy, so the word means to move carefully through a tricky place.
fact: Negotiate means to talk until people reach an agreement.
fact: «A compromise is a deal where each side gets part of what it wants.» Negotiating often leads to a compromise.
fact: Countries negotiate peace, and children negotiate screen time, pocket money and turns with friends.
fact: Negotiate can also mean to get safely past something difficult, like a steep path or a tricky bend.
fact: The forms are negotiate, negotiates, negotiated and negotiating.
exercise: «They negotiated a later bedtime with their parents.» What does negotiated mean here? | Went to bed early | *Talked and agreed to get something | Shouted until everyone went quiet | Hid the clock
exercise: «The bus driver had to negotiate a steep, icy bend.» What does negotiate mean here? | Ignore the bend | *Get safely past the bend | Ask the bend to wait | Paint the bend red
exercise: Ravi and Mia each gave a little so they could agree on a game. What were they doing? | Shouting over each other | Falling asleep | Ignoring each other | *Negotiating a compromise
test: Two countries sat down to negotiate peace. What is the best meaning? | *Talk until they agree | Fight until one side wins | Build a wall between them | Give up and go home
test: Mum and the seller talked until they agreed a price for the bike. They ___ the price. | Painted | Ignored | *Negotiated | Dropped
exam: Which sentence uses negotiate to mean getting safely past something difficult? | *The skier carefully negotiated the steep, icy slope | The class negotiated the new rules together | Tom negotiated a deal with his sister about the TV | They negotiated a price for the pizza
